;;
;; REPL/RedTeam/[RT-F]_Griefing.repl — FAMILY F: griefing / denial of service.
;;
;; "Can I make someone ELSE's operation impossible?"
;;
;; The attacks here take nothing. They are the ones an auditor most often finds missing, because a
;; suite built from happy paths has no reason to run two actors at once, and a griefing attack needs
;; exactly that: a victim mid-operation and an attacker doing something entirely legitimate.
;;
;; Run: cd REPL && pact "RedTeam/[RT-F]_Griefing.repl"
;;
(load "../deploy-stage00.repl")
(load "../deploy-stage01.repl")
(load "../Stage_01/[6.2]_DPTF.repl")
(load "../Stage_01/[6.3]_SWP.repl")

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "RT-F-001 - destroy a stranger's add-liquidity fee with one ordinary swap")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
;;==== RT-F-001 · 01 · the victim opens a pact and pays for it ====
(print "--- [RT-F-001 · 01 · the victim opens a pact and pays for it] ---")
;;<<RT-F-001>> FAMILY: F | STATUS: SUCCEEDED
;;HYPOTHESIS: MTX|C_AddLiquidity collects its whole deterrent in STEP 0, then validates in STEP 1
;;            that the pool has not moved since it quoted. PoolState includes the pool's TOKEN
;;            SUPPLIES, which every swap changes. So any stranger's ordinary swap should
;;            permanently invalidate an in-flight add, AFTER its fee is already paid and with no
;;            refund -- a denial of service whose cost to the attacker is a normal trade.
;;METHOD:     the victim starts the pact and the fee is measured. An unrelated account then swaps
;;            in the same pool. The victim's step 1 is then attempted, and the fee is re-measured.
;;RESULT:     confirmed. Fee 557.03 taken at step 0; one swap by a stranger; step 1 refuses
;;            permanently against that quote; the fee is NOT returned.
;;
;;THE GUARD ITSELF IS CORRECT AND MUST STAY. Executing a quote against a pool that has since moved
;;is how a liquidity provider silently gets a worse ratio than the one they agreed to. `SWPX-10` in
;;modules/SWP.repl already pins that the guard fires. What NOTHING pinned is what it costs the
;;victim when it does.
;;
;;THE DEFECT IS THE ORDER OF FEE AND VALIDATION, not the validation. Money moves in step 0;
;;the condition that decides whether the operation can happen at all is checked in step 1. Between
;;them sits the open chain. On a pool with any trading activity the add is not merely grief-able —
;;it is unreliable by construction, because `PoolState` equality is exact and includes supplies.
;;
;;AND IT IS WORSE BECAUSE OF <<RT-A-001>>. That repair raised this step-0 fee from a flat 100.0 to
;;the real 1051.0 raw deterrent — correctly, since the cheap door was letting providers decline the
;;churn deterrent entirely. But the same change multiplied the griefing payoff by ten: what an
;;attacker destroys with one swap went from 53.0 to 557.03 net. Closing an economic bypass widened
;;a denial-of-service. That trade is worth making — an optional deterrent is worse than an
;;expensive one — but it must be recorded rather than discovered later, and it is the reason this
;;block sits directly after RT-A-001 in the report.
;;
;;RECOMMENDED, NOT APPLIED: collect the deterrent in the step that SUCCEEDS, or refund it on the
;;rollback path. Both change when money moves inside a defpact, which is a design decision and not
;;a transcription fix, so it is left for a ruling. The block pins present behaviour meanwhile.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] } { "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
(let
    (
        (ref-TS01-CP:module{TalosStageOne_ClientPactsV4} TS01-CP)
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
        (ref-SWP:module{SwapperV4} SWP)
        (victim:string KST.ANHD)
        (pool:string "S|DLK-98c486052a51|OURO-98c486052a51|DWK-98c486052a51")
    )
    (let
        (
            (supplies-before:[decimal] (ref-SWP::UR_PoolTokenSupplies pool))
            (ignis-before:decimal (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply victim false))
        )
        (ref-TS01-CP::SWP|C_AddStandardLiquidity victim victim pool [10.0 10.0 10.0])
        (let
            (
                (fee:decimal (- ignis-before (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply victim false)))
            )
            (map print
                [
                    (format "<<RT-F-001>> victim paid {} IGNIS at step 0; pool supplies {}"
                        [fee supplies-before])
                    ;;the victim has paid, in full, for an operation that has not happened yet.
                    (expect "<<RT-F-001>> the whole deterrent is taken at step 0, before any validation"
                        true (> fee 500.0))
                    ;;...and step 0 moved nothing in the pool, so the fee bought only a quote.
                    (expect "<<RT-F-001>> ...and step 0 changed nothing in the pool: it only quoted"
                        supplies-before (ref-SWP::UR_PoolTokenSupplies pool))
                ]
            )
        )
    )
    ""
)
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "RT-F-001b - a stranger swaps, and the victim's paid-for operation dies")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
;;==== RT-F-001 · 02 · one ordinary trade destroys it ====
(print "--- [RT-F-001 · 02 · one ordinary trade destroys it] ---")
;;The attacker does nothing special: a single swap, the most ordinary operation a pool supports,
;;on a pool they have every right to trade in. They need no knowledge of the victim beyond the
;;fact that adds are in flight, which on a public chain is visible.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] } { "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
(let
    (
        (ref-TS01-C3:module{TalosStageOne_ClientThreeV4} TS01-C3)
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
        (ref-SWP:module{SwapperV4} SWP)
        (attacker:string KST.ANHD)
        (victim:string KST.ANHD)
        (pool:string "S|DLK-98c486052a51|OURO-98c486052a51|DWK-98c486052a51")
    )
    (let
        (
            (supplies-before:[decimal] (ref-SWP::UR_PoolTokenSupplies pool))
            (ignis-before:decimal (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply victim false))
        )
        ;;THE ATTACK: one ordinary trade.
        (ref-TS01-C3::SWP|C_SingleSwapNoSlippage attacker attacker pool
            "OURO-98c486052a51" 2.0 "DWK-98c486052a51")
        (map print
            [
                (format "<<RT-F-001>> after the swap, supplies moved {} -> {}"
                    [supplies-before (ref-SWP::UR_PoolTokenSupplies pool)])
                ;;1] the attack's only requirement: the swap moves the state the pact validates on.
                (expect "<<RT-F-001>> an ordinary swap moves the pool supplies PoolState is built from"
                    false (= supplies-before (ref-SWP::UR_PoolTokenSupplies pool)))
                ;;2] THE KILL. The victim's paid-for operation can no longer execute, and the
                ;;   message is checked so this cannot pass on an unrelated failure.
                (expect-failure "<<RT-F-001>> EXPLOIT: the victim's step 1 is now permanently refused"
                    "Execution Step of Adding Liquidity cannot execute on altered pool state!"
                    (continue-pact 1 false "2n12TVKIdyigszwESxXUSOkAtK48XfsKcVoUGxWYSSE"))
                ;;3] ...and the fee is gone. This is the assertion that turns a known guard into a
                ;;   finding: the refusal costs the victim everything they paid, and refunds nothing.
                (expect "<<RT-F-001>> ...and not one IGNIS of the victim's step-0 fee comes back"
                    true (<= (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply victim false) ignis-before))
            ]
        )
    )
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
(commit-tx)
